_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kimkulling/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kimkulling/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-11-07T09:03:49Z","updated_at":"2015-11-07T09:03:49Z","body":"Checked this: the []-operator will return a pointer showing to the first entry of the row of the matrix. I added a test to show this.\nYou can use it as following:\n\n```\nTEST_F( utMatrix4x4Test, indexOperatorTest ) {\n    aiMatrix4x4 m;\n    float *a0 = m[ 0 ];\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 1.0f, *a0 );\n    float *a1 = a0+1;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a1 );\n    float *a2 = a0 + 2;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a2 );\n    float *a3 = a0 + 3;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a3 );\n\n    float *a4 = m[ 1 ];\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a4 );\n    float *a5 = a4 + 1;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 1.0f, *a5 );\n    float *a6 = a4 + 2;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a6 );\n    float *a7 = a4 + 3;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a7 );\n\n    float *a8 = m[ 2 ];\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a8 );\n    float *a9 = a8 + 1;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a9 );\n    float *a10 = a8 + 2;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 1.0f, *a10 );\n    float *a11 = a8 + 3;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a11 );\n\n    float *a12 = m[ 3 ];\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a12 );\n    float *a13 = a12 + 1;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a13 );\n    float *a14 = a12 + 2;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 0.0f, *a14 );\n    float *a15 = a12 + 3;\n    EXPECT_FLOAT_EQ( 1.0f, *a15 );\n}\n```\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/assimp/assimp/issues/comments/154661861/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kimkulling","id":2323156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjMxNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2323156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kimkulling","